"reading-usb-speed-labels":{"description":{"zh":"先换算线速并看两头谈成哪档，再找链条上最窄的一段，最后看它走 USB 桥接还是 PCIe 隧道。","en":"Convert the name to a line rate and check what both ends negotiate, find the narrowest stage, and ask whether it goes through a USB bridge or a PCIe tunnel."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-usb-drives-talk/#ch11","lessons":[{"slug":"how-usb-drives-talk","step":null,"anchor":"ch11","category":"computing","stage":"university","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["移动硬盘参数怎么看","USB 速度标识怎么看","硬盘盒规格怎么看"],"en":["how to read USB speed labels","external drive spec sheet","what to check on a USB enclosure box"]}},
"redis-scan-reverse-cursor":{"description":{"zh":"KEYS * 会阻塞主线程；SCAN 通过位反转递增（从最高位向低位步进），在哈希表翻倍或缩容时仍保证一轮扫描不漏键。","en":"KEYS * stalls the single thread; SCAN reverses bits to increment from MSB down so table doubling or shrinking mid-iteration never misses keys."},"source":"../computing/software/how-redis-answers-in-microseconds/#ch9","lessons":[{"slug":"how-redis-answers-in-microseconds","step":null,"anchor":"ch9","category":"computing","stage":"university","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["redis KEYS * 为什么卡","SCAN 为什么不漏 key","逆二进制游标"],"en":["why SCAN never misses keys","reverse-binary cursor","redis SCAN vs KEYS"]}},
"thunderbolt-summary":{"description":{"zh":"一根 USB-C 线能带多少东西，取决于三层：插座和线缆能过什么，路由器之间谈成了什么，连接管理器怎么分。","en":"What one USB-C cable can carry depends on three layers: what the connector and cable pass, what the routers negotiate, and how the Connection Manager divides it."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-thunderbolt-works/#ch11","lessons":[{"slug":"how-thunderbolt-works","step":null,"anchor":"ch11","category":"computing","stage":"university","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["雷电接口是怎么工作的","雷电接口原理","一根 USB-C 线为什么能接所有东西","雷电是什么","Thunderbolt 是什么","USB-C 能干什么","雷电"],"en":["how Thunderbolt works","what is Thunderbolt","how one USB-C cable carries everything","Thunderbolt explained","what can USB-C do","Thunderbolt"]}},
"ai-nic":{"description":{"zh":"按流哈希选路，几条大流会撞到同一条路；按包喷洒、网卡乱序重组，各条路才一样忙。","en":"Hashing flows onto paths lets a few big flows collide; spraying packets and reordering them in the NIC keeps every path equally busy."},"source":"../computing/systems/how-a-nic-moves-packets/#ch12","lessons":[{"slug":"how-a-nic-moves-packets","step":null,"anchor":"ch12","category":"computing","stage":"university","primary":true}],"aliases":{"zh":["包喷洒","ECMP","等价多路径","PTP 硬件时间戳"],"en":["packet spraying","equal-cost multipath","PTP hardware timestamping"]}},
